Turkish keywords for the Scala compiler (Kojo/Koco).

Generated against the pristine scala/scala v2.13.18 sources, so it applies to a
clean checkout of that tag:

    git clone https://github.com/scala/scala ~/src/scala-2.13.18
    cd ~/src/scala-2.13.18 && git checkout v2.13.18
    git apply <kojo-clone>/scala-tr/turkish-keywords.patch
    java_std_path            # jdk1.8.0_271 -- see scala-tr/README
    sbt dist/mkPack

The change to Main.scala is only a diagnostic println and is not required; the
keywords themselves come from Scanners.scala (the Turkish entries go FIRST in
allKeywords, so compiler errors still report the English keyword) and
StdNames.scala (the keyword strings).

--- a/src/compiler/scala/tools/nsc/Main.scala
+++ b/src/compiler/scala/tools/nsc/Main.scala
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
   override def newCompiler(): Global = Global(settings)
 
   override def doCompile(compiler: Global): Unit = {
+    println("[Kojo] Scala Compiler v2.13.18 with Turkish keywords")
     if (settings.resident.value) resident(compiler)
     else super.doCompile(compiler)
   }
